  "source_hypothesis": "Arbitrary complex Hilbert space; B bounded, fixed and self-adjoint; A(t) bounded, nonnegative, self-adjoint and norm-continuous. The commutator product is bounded by M/10. Compactly supported C1 curves satisfy the solution estimate for TM<1/2 and the positive energy estimate for every T.",
  "component_scope": "An evolution with a nonnegative operator multiplying a fixed self-adjoint operator need not itself be positive. The obstruction is their failure to commute. We bound that obstruction through two ordinary commutators, then obtain both a small-time solution estimate and a positive energy estimate. Every operator acts on an arbitrary complex Hilbert space; no finite-dimensional reduction or spectral gap is assumed.",
  "numbered_displays": 30,
